{{! append-version-delta: formal-methods H2.6c, dal:AppendVersions, dal:RowLevelGuardOnly variant.
    The family's data graph holds every version it has written, and this
    update only adds to it. Nothing is swept and nothing is deleted, so a
    superseded version stays queryable (ADR-A67) and the quadratic fill of a
    replace never applies. The guard is the identity's version row at the
    expected seq, and the txn claim. The new version's own triples arrive in
    the payload slot, and a member the caller does not restate is shared by
    reference, so the payload holds only the new version (VH-Q2). The row's
    current version is the latest one written (VH-D1), and the new version
    is linked to the one it follows with pat:previousVersion when the row names one. Persistence
    never writes fnd:supersededBy, which the domain asserts under its own rule. The
    row also moves its seq and head, and the new version names its receipt
    with pat:revision, as an event does. The first version is written at seq 0
    onto a row bootstrap-version-row created, so it has no prior version.
    Every pattern and the payload sit in the graph the dataGraph slot names,
    and the default graph is never read or written (static check S-1).
    requestDigest is computed by the caller as lower-case hex SHA-256 over
    the tuple-encoded operation kind, target, expected seq and sorted
    canonical N-Triples of the skolemized payload (guide §15.2), and recorded
    on the txn claim.
    dal:DeltaMembership (H2.6f): the new version states what changed since the
    version before it, and does not list its members. addedMembers and
    droppedMembers are request-time Mustache slots holding the triples
    newVersion pat:addsMember m and newVersion pat:dropsMember m, and either may
    be empty. On a checkpoint version, the first and every dal:checkpointEvery-th,
    the caller writes the full list under the domain's membership property and
    newVersion pat:checkpoint true in payloadTriples and leaves both slots empty.
    The members query reads the result, and a domain shape runs over its results.
    payloadTriples, addedMembers and droppedMembers are request-time Mustache slots, not SPARQL variables.
    Note for template authors: never put a Mustache tag inside this
    comment block. Chevron's comment parser ends at the first closing
    double-brace it sees, which silently truncates the comment. }}
PREFIX pat: <https://example.org/lattice/patterns#>
PREFIX xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#>

DELETE {
  GRAPH {{{metaGraphPrefix}}} { $root pat:seq $expectedSeq ; pat:head ?prevRev ; pat:currentVersion ?priorVersion }
}
INSERT {
  GRAPH {{{dataGraph}}} {
      $newVersion pat:revision $newRev .
      $newVersion pat:previousVersion ?priorVersion .
      {{{payloadTriples}}}
      {{{addedMembers}}}
      {{{droppedMembers}}}
  }
  GRAPH {{{metaGraphPrefix}}} { $root pat:epoch $epoch ; pat:seq $nextSeq ; pat:head $newRev ; pat:currentVersion $newVersion }
  GRAPH {{{txnGraph}}}        { $txnId pat:rev $newRev ; pat:requestDigest $requestDigest }
  GRAPH ?logGraph {
      $newRev a pat:Revision ; pat:target $root ; pat:epoch $epoch ; pat:seq $nextSeq ;
              pat:prevRev ?prevRev ; pat:txn ?txnKey ; pat:recordedAt ?now
  }
}
WHERE {
  BIND(IRI(CONCAT(STR({{{logGraphPrefix}}}), SUBSTR(STR(NOW()), 1, 7))) AS ?logGraph)
  GRAPH {{{metaGraphPrefix}}} {
      $root pat:epoch $epoch ; pat:seq $expectedSeq .
      OPTIONAL { $root pat:head ?prevRev }
      OPTIONAL { $root pat:currentVersion ?priorVersion }
      FILTER NOT EXISTS { $root pat:deleted true }
  }
  FILTER NOT EXISTS { GRAPH {{{txnGraph}}} { $txnId pat:rev ?any } }
  BIND(STR($txnId) AS ?txnKey)
  BIND(NOW() AS ?now)
}
